{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Runs every system once on ","type":"text"},{"code":"world","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", running systems that do not depend on each other at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same time.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"run(on:)","externalID":"s:7Systems8ScheduleV3run2ony11WorldModule0E0Vz_tF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Schedule.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Systems\/Schedule.swift#L162"},"role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"world","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A system depends on the systems before it that it must run after, by an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"text":" constraint, and on those it conflicts with: one writes what the other reads or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes, or either has no ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true},{"text":". The systems run in waves: each wave holds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems whose dependencies all ran in earlier waves, and runs them with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)"},{"text":". A system without an access runs alone. The world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends as it would running the systems one after another in order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At the start of each wave, every condition of its systems is checked, so a condition reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only what its system’s access lists, and the world’s change tick advances. Each system’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"WorldModule\/World\/lastRun","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the tick of its previous run, so filters such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".changed(Position.self)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" show it what changed since then: changes made by the systems"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after it on the previous run and before it on this one, but not its own. A system that has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not run on this world before sees every component as added and changed. A skipped system"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has not run: the next time it runs, it sees everything since it last did."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before the first wave, each system that has not run on this world is initialized"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/initialize(in:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Command buffers the wave’s systems queue ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":") apply at the end"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the wave, in the order the systems run. The tick advances once more after the last wave,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so changes made to the world between runs are newer than every system’s previous run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every system with an access reads and writes only what it lists; see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"defaultImplementations":1,"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Access","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","abstract":[{"text":"What the system reads and writes, so ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},{"text":" can run it alongside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems it does not conflict with; nil, the default, when it may change anything and must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run alone.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"role":"collection","title":"Systems","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Rules that run on a world, in the order written unless constrained otherwise.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/run(on:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"on","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/run(on:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs every system once on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":", running systems that do not depend on each other at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"run(on:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/run(on:)"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Entities, the components they hold, and the world’s resources.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"World","role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/initialize(in:)":{"defaultImplementations":1,"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"initialize"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V","text":"World"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/initialize(in:)","title":"initialize(in:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prepares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world"},{"type":"text","text":" for the system, before its first run on it: a schedule calls this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before the wave the system first runs in, outside any concurrent run. Nothing, by default."}],"required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/initialize(in:)"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","title":"Schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems that run on a world, as though in the order written, at the same time where they can."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"}}}